Rebased onto upstream Mesa 76b9372c4e5d186f57d22d3a4f95dd1c5e04ece2.
Only the host program-state reference change is imported. No ARMSX2
feedback-loop coherency relaxation, barriers, shader capabilities, GPU
identity or clock constraints are imported. All current consumers were
updated; unbound command buffers use static zero state as before.

Only PERF_PROFILE=sd865-program-reference applies the patch. Both SD865
profiles use Android API 29, android-strict=false and identical O3/A77/ThinLTO
flags. android-strict=false permits exposing implemented Vulkan features
beyond Android's API-level whitelist; it does not implement or force-enable
unsupported GPU features. The A650 Vulkan feature gates remain upstream's.

The 10KB copy figure and PS2 CPU measurements are the origin author's
observations, not measured FF7R gains. Compile, package and S20+ acceptance
are separate gates. Pipeline lifetime must obey Vulkan's existing recording
and submission rules, as for every other borrowed pipeline/shader pointer.

